124
00:08:57.522 --> 00:09:01.957
are sufficient. From this inventory, a
traceable checklist uses P-01

125
00:09:01.957 --> 00:09:06.391
for eye protection, closed-toe footwear,
supervisor confirmation, immediate damage

126
00:09:06.391 --> 00:09:10.826
reporting, and the prohibition on
operating damaged equipment. S-01 triggers

127
00:09:10.826 --> 00:09:15.261
follow-up because it reports the
equipment-room guard as damaged. N-01

128
00:09:15.261 --> 00:09:19.696
explains the delayed inspection but
changes no rule. I-01 corroborates

129
00:09:19.696 --> 00:09:24.130
only visible words. The policy version,
inspection result, damaged-guard report,

130
00:09:24.130 --> 00:09:28.565
and supervisor confirmation belong in a
controlled system of record,

131
00:09:28.565 --> 00:09:33.000
not only in chat history.

132
00:09:33.000 --> 00:09:37.360
A complete compact packet is more than a
short summary.

133
00:09:37.360 --> 00:09:41.720
It states the objective: draft a short
equipment-room entry checklist

134
00:09:41.720 --> 00:09:46.080
